  <section><p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> Telegram has <strong>over 1 billion</strong> monthly active users in 2026, with <strong>15 million+</strong> Premium subscribers (roughly 1.5%). The company turned its first profit in 2024 ($547M), grew H1 2025 revenue to $870M (+65%), but also posted a $220M+ net loss over that same half-year because of a Toncoin write-down. Every number below is dated and sourced.</p></section>

  <section><h2>How many users does Telegram have?</h2><p>Telegram founder Pavel Durov <a href="https://x.com/durov/status/1902454590747902091" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">announced on X</a> on March 20, 2025, that Telegram had reached "significantly over 1 billion monthly active users" — making it the world's second most-used messaging app after WhatsApp, excluding China-specific WeChat.</p><p>In the same announcement, Durov shared engagement figures: the average user opens the app <strong>21 times a day</strong> and spends <strong>41 minutes a day</strong> in it. Third-party analytics platforms estimate daily active users at roughly <strong>500 million</strong> — half of MAU, a notably strong ratio (an estimate, not an official Telegram figure).</p></section>

  <section><h2>How many Telegram Premium subscribers are there?</h2><div class="post-table-wrap"><table class="post-table"><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Premium subscribers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>December 2023</td><td>4 million</td></tr><tr><td>September 2024</td><td>10 million</td></tr><tr><td>December 2024</td><td>12 million</td></tr><tr><td>May 2025</td><td>15 million+</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>In May 2025, Durov <a href="https://x.com/durov/status/1927460225461662111" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">posted on X</a>: "Telegram Premium now has over 15 million paid subscribers," noting the number had doubled in a single year. 15 million is about <strong>1.5%</strong> of the 1-billion MAU base — still a small slice, but a segment that has nearly quadrupled in 18 months.</p><p>For what Premium actually includes and how the plans compare, see <a href="/en/blog/telegram-premium-features">what Telegram Premium actually gives you</a>.</p></section>

  <section><h2>How much revenue does Telegram make?</h2><div class="post-table-wrap"><table class="post-table"><thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2024 (full year)</td><td>Total revenue</td><td>$1B+</td></tr><tr><td>2024 (full year)</td><td>Net profit</td><td>$547M (first profitable year)</td></tr><tr><td>H1 2025</td><td>Revenue</td><td>$870M (+65% YoY)</td></tr><tr><td>H1 2025</td><td>Net result</td><td>$220M+ loss (Toncoin write-down)</td></tr><tr><td>2025 (target)</td><td>Full-year revenue</td><td>$2B (per FT reporting)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>In December 2024, Durov <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2024/12/23/pavel-durov-says-telegram-is-now-profitable" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">officially announced</a> that annual revenue had surpassed $1 billion and net profit reached $547 million — the company's first profitable year. It closed the year with over $500 million in cash, and a meaningful share of the roughly $2 billion in bonds issued over four years was repaid that autumn.</p><p>The picture shifted in H1 2025. Per Financial Times reporting, revenue rose from $525M (H1 2024) to $870M (+65%), with the company targeting $2 billion for the full year. But after Toncoin lost 69% of its value in 2025 (per CoinGecko) and Telegram sold over $450 million of it, the company posted a <strong>net loss of $220M+</strong> in H1 2025 — versus a $334M profit in H1 2024. That swing shows how much of Telegram's bottom line still depends on crypto-asset prices.</p></section>

  <section><h2>How much do Stars cost internationally?</h2><p>Buying Telegram Stars directly through the App Store or Google Play is priced in US dollars and requires an internationally-billed card:</p><div class="post-table-wrap"><table class="post-table"><thead><tr><th>Stars</th><th>App Store price (approx., 2026)</th><th>StarsJoy price (UZS)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 Stars</td><td>$1.99</td><td>24,000 UZS</td></tr><tr><td>1,000 Stars</td><td>$14.99</td><td>240,000 UZS</td></tr><tr><td>10,000 Stars</td><td>$134.99</td><td>2,400,000 UZS</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>App Store and Google Play pricing is out of reach for most buyers in Uzbekistan, since it needs an internationally-billed Visa or Mastercard. StarsJoy solves that: pay directly in som with Uzcard or Humo, at a flat <strong>240 UZS per star</strong> for any quantity. See the full price table at <a href="/en/stars">Buy Telegram Stars</a>.</p></section>

  <section><h2>How much do creators actually earn from Stars?</h2><p>When a channel or bot owner cashes out earned Stars, industry estimates put the payout at roughly <strong>$0.013 per Star</strong> when the buyer purchased on web or desktop. If the buyer purchases inside the iOS or Android app instead, Apple or Google take a 30% cut, and the payout drops to around <strong>$0.009 per Star</strong>.</p><p>That gap is why many channel and bot owners tell their audience to buy Stars through the web version rather than in-app. See <a href="/en/blog/what-you-can-do-with-telegram-stars">what you can actually do with Telegram Stars</a> for the full range of ways Stars get earned and spent.</p></section>

  <section><h2>How big is the Telegram Gifts market?</h2><p>Third-party market data puts total Telegram Gifts trading volume at over <strong>$354 million</strong> since launch (as of March 2026). As of November 2025, more than 2 million users collectively owned over 9 million digital gifts. Upgrading an ordinary gift into a unique NFT version costs just <strong>25 Stars</strong> — the TON network fee.</p><p>These figures describe the overall market; for record prices on individual gifts, see <a href="/en/blog/most-expensive-telegram-gifts">the most expensive Telegram gifts in 2026</a>.</p></section>
